An audit asks one question per kind of problem, answers it with code, and writes down why it matters for a decision . Run every check on the raw file before changing anything, so you know what you are about to fix: Are there duplicate bookings? Are hotels and channels spelled consistently ? Are there impossible rates ? Are there impossible lead times or rooms without adults ? What is missing ? Checks 1 and 2. duplicated() marks a row identical, column by column, to an earlier one; value_counts() lists every distinct text and how often it appears. At the bottom, one booking that was loaded twice. In [8]: Copied! print ( f "Exact duplicate rows: { raw . duplicated () . sum () } 
